# Docker build context is the REPO ROOT (see render.yaml: dockerContext: .).
# Without this file the context includes ~3.5 GB of local-only artifacts.

# Virtualenvs / node deps — reinstalled inside the image
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules

# Python bytecode & caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Next.js build output — the frontend is NOT part of the backend image
frontend/.next
frontend/out

# VCS & editor
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Local runtime state — the Render Disk supplies these at /app/backend/data
backend/data
backend/datasets
backend/logs
*.log
**/mlruns

# NOTE: backend/src/utils/.sessions/*.json is deliberately NOT excluded — the
# Playwright scrapers read it for authenticated social scraping, and the original
# image shipped it too. It DOES mean live account cookies are baked into the
# image layer. See DEPLOY.md "Security".

# Secrets — injected as Render env vars, never baked into the image
.env
**/.env

# Docs / assets not needed at runtime
*.pdf
DEPLOY.md
demo
